# Cell from playpick: mode=walk, boss=skyward, spec=paladin:retribution,
# style=idle, size=25, difficulty=heroic, view=844x390,touch, save=carried.
#
# skyward (The Skyward Deck) is the last built encounter before the throne
# (src/sim/encounters.ts order: marrow, whisper, host, gorged, confluence,
# flasks, crowns, gift, saved, cold, skyward) and carries the single widest
# played-vs-idle gap in the whole balance table (docs/upkeep.md: 76% played /
# 6% idle, +70). An `evening` does not steer toward a named boss though --
# "it needs no map and no door to aim at" -- so `boss` here is a coverage
# label, not a target: this walks in at the door in whatever order the
# building gives, same as every other mode=walk session so far.
#
# What is actually new: no prior session has run `idle` inside `evening` at
# all (checked the ledger directly -- `idle` has only ever been used twice,
# both single mode=raid pulls, never mode=walk or mode=clear). Style only
# matters once inside a boss room though: `scripts/playbot.ts`'s `evening()`
# calls `cross()` for a travel-mode room and `cross()` takes no style
# argument at all -- corridors, including THE VIGIL (direction.md #6/#281),
# are walked exactly the same way regardless of what style was assigned.
# So this session doubles as a check of that reading: if VIGIL stalls again,
# it should stall at essentially the same spot the wander/good/wander trio
# in #281 already found, since idle's corridor behaviour is not idle at all
# -- only its behaviour once inside an actual fight room is.
#
# carried is very likely to behave as fresh here regardless (open bug #273:
# a new port every separate playbot invocation means a new localStorage
# origin), so size/difficulty are expected to come up locked and the setup
# screen's own default (10-normal) substituted, the same way every earlier
# session on a fresh-acting save has gone.
